<title>USA: Provident Cos Inc Q3 net rises slightly.</title>
<headline>Provident Cos Inc Q3 net rises slightly.</headline>
<dateline>CHATTANOOGA, Tenn. 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.66		    $0.66</p>
<p> Net			 33,200		   32,900</p>
<p> Revs		     566,800		  603,600</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  45,551		   45,389</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>			9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $2.03		    $1.56</p>
<p> Net			101,700		   80,200</p>
<p> Revs		   1,733,400		1,990,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  45,498		   45,378</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1995 nine month figures include gain on sale of group medical business, which increased after-tax operating earnings by $0.31 per share.</p>
<p>Revenue figures are before net realized investment losses.</p>
<p>Income before net realized investment losses was $36 million vs $33.4 million in Q3 and $108.2 million vs $99.2 million for nine months.</p>
<p>Income per share before net realized investment losses $0.72 vs $0.67 for Q3 and $2.17 vs $1.98 for nine mos.</p>
</text>
